From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 19:37:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lineage: add msm8992/msm8994 to QCOM_BOARD_PLATFORMS

Companion to the B64_FAMILY restore. That patch fixed CAF tree selection in
config/BoardConfigQcom.mk; this fixes is-vendor-board-platform, which is a
different variable in a different file (build/core/vendor/qcom_boards.mk) and
was still missing every pre-UM platform.

The failure mode is quiet, which is what makes it worth calling out: modules
gated on $(call is-vendor-board-platform,QCOM) are simply never defined, so
there is no error where the gating happens. It only surfaces at the end of
the makefile parse as 'includes non-existent modules in PRODUCT_PACKAGES',
naming libbt-vendor, android.hardware.power-service-qti and friends with no
hint as to why they vanished.
---
 build/core/vendor/qcom_boards.mk | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/core/vendor/qcom_boards.mk b/build/core/vendor/qcom_boards.mk
index 33b6ecb5..4f49c819 100644
--- a/build/core/vendor/qcom_boards.mk
+++ b/build/core/vendor/qcom_boards.mk
@@ -15,6 +15,20 @@ TARO := taro #SM8450
 PARROT := parrot #SM6450
 KALAMA := kalama #SM8550
 
+# B64 Family — restored for the ether (Nextbit Robin) port.
+# lineage-20.0 dropped every pre-UM legacy family from this list. msm8992 is not in
+# QCOM_BOARD_PLATFORMS, so $(call is-vendor-board-platform,QCOM) returns false, which
+# silently gates out whole components rather than erroring: libbt-vendor (Bluetooth),
+# android.hardware.power-service-qti (the power HAL the perf tuning drives), and the
+# QCOM data/crypto pieces. They then surface only as "non-existent modules in
+# PRODUCT_PACKAGES" at the very end of the makefile parse.
+#
+# This is separate from the B64_FAMILY restore in config/BoardConfigQcom.mk: that one
+# selects the CAF hardware variant (msm8992 shares msm8994's trees), while this list
+# is what is-vendor-board-platform tests. Both are needed.
+QCOM_BOARD_PLATFORMS += msm8992
+QCOM_BOARD_PLATFORMS += msm8994
+
 # UM Family
 QCOM_BOARD_PLATFORMS += msm8937
 QCOM_BOARD_PLATFORMS += msm8953
